{% comment %}
  ==================================================================
  GS PRICE
  ==================================================================
  NAMED gs-price, NOT price. Dawn ships its own snippets/price.liquid.

  USAGE:
    render 'gs-price', cardProduct: product
    render 'gs-price', cardProduct: product, cardVariant: variant
    render 'gs-price', cardProduct: product, hideComparePrice: true
    render 'gs-price', cardProduct: product, savePercentoff: false

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  REVISION 2026-08-13 (2) - THE PRICE WAS NEVER RENDERING
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  This snippet opened with:

      {% raw %}{% if settings.product_price and price %}{% endraw %}

  `settings.product_price` is a gs-shopify-v3 THEME SETTING. It does not
  exist in Dawn's config/settings_schema.json, so it evaluates to nil -
  and the entire price block never rendered. On any page. The product
  page showed a title, stars, swatches and sizes with NO PRICE.

  This is a whole class of defect in this port, not one line. The card
  stack references around a dozen v3 settings that Dawn has no schema
  for - quickview, compare, new_label, sale_label, enable_color_swatches,
  show_countdown, product_second_image, show_savings, product_vendor,
  show_inventory. Every one is undefined, so every feature gated on one
  was silently off.

  THE RULE NOW: a missing setting means ENABLED, not disabled. Each is
  tested with an explicit `== false` so an absent schema entry fails
  open. When those settings are added to settings_schema.json they will
  start controlling behaviour without any change here.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  REVISION 2026-08-13 (1)
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  - FILTER APPLIED TO THE WRONG VALUE:
        {{ raw }}{{ 'products...from_price_html' | t: price: price | money }}{{ endraw }}
    Liquid applies filters left to right, so `money` ran on the OUTPUT of
    `t`. Money values are precomputed with assign now.
  - The snippet now carries gs-price.css. Those rules lived only in
    gs-card-product.css, which loads when a CARD renders, so the price
    was unstyled on the PDP.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  BUGS FIXED FROM v3
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  - Hardcoded `default: 1899` fallback - a magic $18.99 in the price
    renderer.
  - `current_variant` referenced but never assigned; unit pricing
    rendered empty markup on every card. Now an explicit cardVariant.
  - A hidden preorder <span> emitted on every card.
  - Leftover `kea-testing` class. The data-sl-* Shoplift attributes are
    kept - those are live test hooks.
  - `if savePercentoff != false` - unset it is nil, and nil != false is
    TRUE in Liquid, so it silently defaulted on.
  - Compare-at price and the savings badge shared one `unless`, so
    hiding one hid the other.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  KNOWN LIMITATION - A DECISION, NOT A BUG
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Percent-off uses Liquid integer division, which truncates: 33.7%
  displays as 33%, always rounding in the customer's disfavour.
  Preserved as v3 had it. Confirm with Megan before changing.
  ==================================================================
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  unless cardProduct
    break
  endunless

  assign price = cardProduct.price_min
  assign compare_at_price = cardProduct.compare_at_price_min

  # Missing setting means enabled. See the header note.
  assign show_price = true
  if settings.product_price == false
    assign show_price = false
  endif

  assign show_savings = true
  if settings.show_savings == false
    assign show_savings = false
  endif
  if savePercentoff == false
    assign show_savings = false
  endif

  assign on_sale = false
  if compare_at_price > price
    assign on_sale = true
  endif

  # Precomputed. Passing `price: price | money` into a translation
  # applies money to the translation's OUTPUT, not to price.
  assign price_money = price | money
  assign compare_money = compare_at_price | money
  assign saving_money = compare_at_price | minus: price | money
-%}

{%- if show_price and price -%}
  {{ 'gs-price.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  <div class="product-price{% if on_sale %} product-price--on-sale{% endif %}">
    {%- if cardProduct.price_varies -%}
      <span class="price-item actual-price price-varies" data-sl-attribute-p="{{ cardProduct.id }}">
        {{- 'products.product.price.from_price_html' | t: price: price_money -}}
      </span>
    {%- else -%}
      <span class="price-item actual-price" data-sl-attribute-p="{{ cardProduct.id }}">
        {{- price_money -}}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- unless hideComparePrice -%}
      {%- if on_sale -%}
        <span class="price-item compare-price" data-sl-attribute-cap="{{ cardProduct.id }}">
          {{- compare_money -}}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endunless -%}

    {%- if cardVariant.unit_price_measurement -%}
      <span class="product-unit-price" data-unit-price data-sl-attribute-p="{{ cardProduct.id }}">
        {{- cardVariant.unit_price | money }} /
        {%- if cardVariant.unit_price_measurement.reference_value != 1 -%}
          {{ cardVariant.unit_price_measurement.reference_value }}
        {%- endif -%}
        {{ cardVariant.unit_price_measurement.reference_unit -}}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if show_savings and on_sale -%}
      <span class="product-percent-off" data-sl-attribute-discount="{{ cardProduct.id }}">
        {%- if settings.sale_label_type == 'amount-off' -%}
          {{- saving_money }} {{ 'products.product.badges.off' | t -}}
        {%- else -%}
          {{- compare_at_price | minus: price | times: 100 | divided_by: compare_at_price -}}%
          {{ 'products.product.badges.off' | t -}}
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
